{
  "title": "Ziyarat of Hamzah (a.s.) and the Martyrs of Uhud",
  "data": "Ziyarat of Hamzah (a.s.)\nStanding at the tomb of Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib, recite:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا عَمَّ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA A'MMA RASOOLILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O uncle of Allah’s Messenger,\nصَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهِ\nSALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIH\npeace be upon him and his Household.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا خَيْرَ الشُّهَدَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA KHAYRASH SHUHADAA'\nPeace be upon you, O best of martyrs.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَاۤ اَسَدَ اللّٰهِ وَاَسَدَ رَسُوْلِهٖ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA ASADALLAAHI WA ASADA RASOOLIH\nPeace be upon you, O Lion of Allah and of His Messenger.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ قَدْ جَاهَدْتَ فِي اللّٰهِ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ\nASH-HADU ANNAKA QAD JAAHADTA FILLAAHI A'ZZA WA JALL\nI bear witness that you strove in the way of Allah—the All-mighty and All-majestic—,\nوَجُدْتَ بِنَفْسِكَ\nWA JUDTA BINAFSIK\nsacrificed yourself,\nوَنَصَحْتَ رَسُوْلَ اللّٰهِ\nWA NASAHTA RASOOLALLAAH\nacted sincerely towards Allah’s Messenger,\nصَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهِ\nSALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIH\npeace be upon him and his Household,\nوَكُنْتَ فِيْمَا عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ سُبْحَانَهٗ رَاغِبًا\nWA KUNTA FEEMAA I'NDALLAAHI SUBHAANAHOO RAAGHIBAA\nand desired sincerely for that which is possessed by Allah, the Glorified.\nبِاَبِيْۤ اَنْتَ وَاُمِّيْۤ\nBI-ABEE ANTA WA UMMEE\nMay Allah accept my father and mother as ransoms for you!\nاَتَيْتُكَ مُتَقَرِّبًا اِلَى اللّٰهِ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ بِزِيَارَتِكَ\nATAYTUKA MUTAQARRIBAN ILALLAAHI A'ZZA WA JALLA BIZIYAARATIK\nI have come to you seeking nearness to Allah, the All-mighty and All-majestic, through visiting your tomb,\nوَمُتَقَرِّبًا اِلٰى رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ\nWA MUTAQARRIBAN ILAA RASOOLILLAAH\nand seeking nearness to Allah’s Messenger,\nصَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهٖ بِذٰلِكَ\nSALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIHEE BIDHAALIK\npeace be upon him and his Household, through visiting your tomb, too.\nرَاغِبًا اِلَيْكَ فِي الشَّفَاعَةِ\nRAAGHIBAN ILAYKA FISH SHAFAA'AH\nI thus carry the desire that you may intercede for me.\nاَبْتَغِيْ بِزِيَارَتِكَ خَلَاصَ نَفْسِيْ\nABTAGHEE BIZIYAARATIKA KHALAASA NAFSEE\nThrough my visiting you, I also desire for redemption of myself,\nمُتَعَوِّذًا بِكَ مِنْ نَارٍ اسْتَحَقَّهَا مِثْلِيْ\nMUTA'AWWIDHAN BIKA MIN NAARINIS TAHAQQAHAA MITHLEE\nseeking your protection against the Fire that is deserved by my matches\nبِمَا جَنَيْتُ عَلٰى نَفْسِيْ\nBIMAA JANAYTU A'LAA NAFSEE\nfor what I have done against myself,\nهَارِبًا مِنْ ذُنُوْبِيَ الَّتِي احْتَطَبْتُهَا عَلٰى ظَهْرِيْ\nHAARIBAN MIN DHUNOOBIYAL LATIH TATABTUHAA A'LAA ZAHREE\nfleeing from my sins that I have gathered on my shoulders,\nفَزِعًا اِلَيْكَ رَجَاۤءَ رَحْمَةِ رَبِّيْۤ\nFAZI'AN ILAYKA RAJAA'A RAHMATI RABBEE\nand turning to you for security, in the hope of gaining the mercy of my Lord.\nاَتَيْتُكَ مِنْ شُقَّةٍ بَعِيْدَةٍ\nATAYTUKA MIN SHUQQATIN BA'EEDAH\nI have come to you from a far distance,\nطَالِبًا فَكَاكَ رَقَبَتِيْ مِنَ النَّارِ\nTAALIBAN FAKAAKA RAQABATEE MINAN NAAR\nseeking for release of my neck (i.e. self) from Hellfire\nوَقَدْ اَوْقَرَتْ ظَهْرِيْ ذُنُوْبِيْ\nWA QAD AWQARAT ZAHREE DHUNOOBEE\nalthough I have overburdened my back with my sins\nوَاَتَيْتُ مَاۤ اَسْخَطَ رَبِّيْ\nWA ATAYTU MAA ASKHATA RABBEE\nand I have committed that which enrages my Lord.\nوَلَمْ اَجِدْ اَحَدًا اَفْزَعُ اِلَيْهِ\nWA LAM AJID AHADAN AFZA'U ILAYH\nI cannot find anyone to whom I may resort\nخَيْرًا لِيْ مِنْكُمْ اَهْلَ بَيْتِ الرَّحْمَةِ\nKHAYRAN LEE MINKUM AHLA BAYTIR RAHMAH\nbetter than you, the Household of Mercy;\nفَكُنْ لِيْ شَفِيْعًا يَوْمَ فَقْرِيْ وَحَاجَتِيْ\nFAKUN LEE SHAFEE'AN YAWMA FAQREE WA HAAJATEE\nso, (please) intercede for me on the day of my poverty and neediness,\nفَقَدْ سِرْتُ اِلَيْكَ مَحْزُوْنًا\nFAQAD SIRTU ILAYKA MAHZOONAA\nfor I have walked to you aggrieved,\nوَاَتَيْتُكَ مَكْرُوْبًا\nWA ATAYTUKA MAKROOBAA\nI have come to you distressed,\nوَسَكَبْتُ عَبْرَتِيْ عِنْدَكَ بَاكِيًا\nWA SAKABTU A'BRATEE I'NDAKA BAAKIYAA\nI have shed tears in your presence,\nوَصِرْتُ اِلَيْكَ مُفْرَدًا\nWA SIRTU ILAYKA MUFRADAA\nand I am now alone before you.\nوَاَنْتَ مِمَّنْ اَمَرَنِيَ اللّٰهُ بِصِلَتِهٖ\nWA ANTA MIMMAN AMARANIYALLAAHU BISILATIH\nYou are of those with whom Allah has ordered me to build unbreakable ties,\nوَحَثَّنِيْ عَلٰى بِرِّهٖ\nWA HATHTHANEE A'LAA BIRRIH\nHe has urged me to obey,\nوَدَلَّنِيْ عَلٰى فَضْلِهٖ\nWA DALLANEE A'LAA FADLIH\nHe has shown me your merits,\nوَهَدَانِيْ لِحُبِّهٖ\nWA HADAANEE LIHUBBIH\nHe has guided me to the love for you,\nوَرَغَّبَنِيْ فِي الْوِفَادَةِ اِلَيْهِ\nWA RAGHGHABANEE FIL WIFAADATI ILAYH\nHe has encouraged me to get to you,\nوَاَلْهَمَنِيْ طَلَبَ الْحَوَاۤئِجِ عِنْدَهٗ\nWA ALHAMANEE TALABAL HAWAA'IJI I'NDAH\nand He has inspired me to seek the settlement of my needs at your tombs.\nاَنْتُمْ اَهْلُ بَيْتٍ لَا يَشْقٰى مَنْ تَوَلَّاكُمْ\nANTUM AHLU BAYTIN LAA YASHQAA MAN TAWALLAAKUM\nAs for you the Ahl al-Bayt (the Household of the Prophet), whoever pays homage to you shall never encounter unhappiness,\nوَلَا يَخِيْبُ مَنْ اَتَاكُمْ\nWA LAA YAKHEEBU MAN ATAAKUM\nwhoever comes to you shall never be disappointed,\nوَلَا يَخْسَرُ مَنْ يَهْوَاكُمْ\nWA LAA YAKHSARU MAN YAHWAAKUM\nand whoever loves you shall never fail,\nوَلَا يَسْعَدُ مَنْ عَادَاكُمْ\nWA LAA YAS'ADU MAN A'ADAAKUM\nbut whoever provokes the hostility of you shall never be pleased.\nThen face the qiblah and pray two rak'at. After the prayer, lean over the tomb and recite:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nO Allah, (please do) send blessings upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْ تَعَرَّضْتُ لِرَحْمَتِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE TA'ARRADTU LIRAHMATIK\nO Allah, I expose myself to Your mercy\nبِلُزُوْمِيْ لِقَبْرِ عَمِّ نَبِيِّكَ\nBILUZOOMEE LIQABRI A'MMI NABIYYIK\nas I attach myself to the tomb of Your Prophet’s uncle,\nصَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهِ\nSALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIH\npeace be upon Your Prophet and his Household\nلِيُجِيْرَنِيْ مِنْ نِقْمَتِكَ وَسَخَطِكَ وَمَقْتِكَ\nLIYUJEERANEE MIN NIQMATIKA WA SAKHATIKA WA MAQTIK\nso that he (i.e. Your Prophet’s uncle) may rescue me from Your chastisement, Your wrath, and Your ire\nفِيْ يَوْمٍ تَكْثُرُ فِيْهِ الْاَصْوَاتُ\nFEE YAWMIN TAKTHURU FEEHIL ASWAAT\non the day when cries will be great in number,\nوَتَشْغَلُ كُلُّ نَفْسٍ بِمَا قَدَّمَتْ\nWA TASHGHALU KULLU NAFSIN BIMAA QADDAMAT\nwhen each soul will be engaged with what it has sent before,\nوَتُجَادِلُ عَنْ نَفْسِهَا\nWA TUJAADILU A'N NAFSIHAA\nand each soul will plead for itself.\nفَاِنْ تَرْحَمْنِي الْيَوْمَ فَلَا خَوْفٌ عَلَيَّ وَلَا حُزْنٌ\nFA-IN TARHAMNIL YAWMA FALAA KHAWFUN A'LAYYA WA LAA HUZN\nIf You have mercy upon me on that day, then neither fear nor grief shall come upon me.\nوَاِنْ تُعَاقِبْ فَمَوْلًى لَهُ الْقُدْرَةُ عَلٰى عَبْدِهٖ\nWA IN TU'AAQIB FAMAWLAN LAHUL QUDRATU A'LAA A'BDIH\nBut if You punish me, then You are the Master Who has full power over His slave.\nوَلَا تُخَيِّبْنِيْ بَعْدَ الْيَوْمِ\nWA LAA TUKHAYYIBNEE BA'DAL YAWM\nPlease, do not disappoint me any more after this day\nوَلَا تَصْرِفْنِيْ بِغَيْرِ حَاجَتِيْ\nWA LAA TASRIFNEE BIGHAYRI HAAJATEE\nand do not cause me to leave without having my requests granted.\nفَقَدْ لَصِقْتُ بِقَبْرِ عَمِّ نَبِيِّكَ\nFAQAD LASIQTU BIQABRI A'MMI NABIYYIK\nI have attached myself to the tomb of Your Prophet’s uncle\nوَتَقَرَّبْتُ بِهٖ اِلَيْكَ ابْتِغَاۤءَ مَرْضَاتِكَ\nWA TAQARRABTU BIHEE ILAYKAB TIGHAA'A MARDAATIK\nand I have sought nearness to You through him in the hope of gaining Your pleasure\nوَرَجَاۤءَ رَحْمَتِكَ\nWA RAJAA'A RAHMATIK\nand in the desire of winning Your mercy.\nفَتَقَبَّلْ مِنِّيْ\nFATAQABBAL MINNEE\nSo, (please) accept from me\nوَعُدْ بِحِلْمِكَ عَلٰى جَهْلِيْ\nWA U'D BIHILMIKA A'LAA JAHLEE\nand confer upon my unreason with Your forbearance\nوَبِرَاْفَتِكَ عَلٰى جِنَايَةِ نَفْسِيْ\nWA BIRA'FATIKA A'LAA JINAAYATI NAFSEE\nand upon my mistreatment against myself with Your kindness.\nفَقَدْ عَظُمَ جُرْمِيْ\nFAQAD A'ZUMA JURMEE\nMy offenses are too great;\nوَمَاۤ اَخَافُ اَنْ تَظْلِمَنِيْ\nWA MAA AKHAAFU AN TAZLIMANEE\nyet, I do not anticipate that You may wrong me,\nوَلٰكِنْ اَخَافُ سُوْۤءَ الْحِسَابِ\nWA LAAKIN AKHAAFU SOO'AL HISAAB\nbut I anticipate terrible reckoning.\nفَانْظُرِ الْيَوْمَ تَقَلُّبِيْ عَلٰى قَبْرِ عَمِّ نَبِيِّكَ\nFANZURIL YAWMA TAQALLUBEE A'LAA QABRI A'MMI NABIYYIK\nSo, (please) on this day, notice my turning on the tomb of Your Prophet’s uncle;\nفَبِهِمَا فُكَّنِيْ مِنَ النَّارِ\nFABIHIMAA FUKKANEE MINAN NAAR\nand, in the names of both of them (i.e. the Holy Prophet and his uncle), release me from Hellfire,\nوَلَا تُخَيِّبْ سَعْيِيْ\nWA LAA TUKHAYYIB SA'YEE\ndo not frustrate my efforts,\nوَلَا يَهُوْنَنَّ عَلَيْكَ ابْتِهَالِيْ\nWA LAA YAHOONANNA A'LAYKAB TIHAALEE\ndo not belittle my invocation to You,\nوَلَا تَحْجُبَنَّ عَنْكَ صَوْتِيْ\nWA LAA TAHJUBANNA A'NKA SAWTEE\ndo not cause my voice not to reach You,\nوَلَا تَقْلِبْنِيْ بِغَيْرِ حَوَاۤئِجِيْ\nWA LAA TAQLIBNEE BIGHAYRI HAWAA'IJEE\nand do not make me leave (this place) without having my needs settled for me.\nيَا غِيَاثَ كُلِّ مَكْرُوْبٍ وَمَحْزُوْنٍ\nYAA GHIYAATHA KULLI MAKROOBIN WA MAHZOON\nO Succor of all aggrieved and saddened ones!\nوَيَا مُفَرِّجًا عَنِ الْمَلْهُوْفِ الْحَيْرَانِ\nWA YAA MUFARRIJAN A'NIL MALHOOFIL HAYRAAN\nO Reliever of the grieved, confused,\nالْغَرِيْقِ الْمُشْرِفِ عَلَى الْهَلَكَةِ\nAL-GHAREEQIL MUSHRIFI A'LAL HALAKAH\ndrowned, and perishable ones!\nفَصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nFASALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\n(Please) send blessings upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَانْظُرْ اِلَيَّ نَظْرَةً لَا اَشْقٰى بَعْدَهَا اَبَدًا\nWANZUR ILAYYA NAZRATAN LAA ASHQAA BA'DAHAA ABADAA\nsend to me a look (from You) that saves me from unhappiness forever,\nوَارْحَمْ تَضَرُّعِيْ وَعَبْرَتِيْ وَانْفِرَادِيْ\nWARHAM TADARRU'EE WA A'BRATEE WANFIRAADEE\nand have mercy upon my obtestation, tears, and loneliness.\nفَقَدْ رَجَوْتُ رِضَاكَ\nFAQAD RAJAWTU RIDAAK\nI do hope for Your pleasure\nوَتَحَرَّيْتُ الْخَيْرَ الَّذِيْ لَا يُعْطِيْهِ اَحَدٌ سِوَاكَ\nWA TAHARRAYTUL KHAYRAL LADHEE LAA YU'TEEHI AHADUN SIWAAK\nand I seek for the good that none save You can provide;\nفَلَا تَرُدَّ اَمَلِيْ\nFALAA TARUDDA AMALEE\nso please do not disappoint me.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنْ تُعَاقِبْ فَمَوْلًى لَهُ الْقُدْرَةُ عَلٰى عَبْدِهٖ\nALLAAHUMMA IN TU'AAQIB FAMAWLAN LAHUL QUDRATU A'LAA A'BDIH\nO Allah, if You punish me, then You are the Master Who has full power over His slave\nوَجَزَاۤئِهٖ بِسُوْۤءِ فِعْلِهٖ\nWA JAZAA'IHEE BISOO'I FI'LIH\nand it is naught but my misdeeds that pulled me to Your punishment,\nفَلَاۤ اَخِيْبَنَّ الْيَوْمَ\nFALAA AKHEEBANNAL YAWM\nbut I beg You not to disappoint me this day,\nوَلَا تَصْرِفْنِيْ بِغَيْرِ حَاجَتِيْ\nWA LAA TASRIFNEE BIGHAYRI HAAJATEE\nnot to make me leave without having my needs settled for me,\nوَلَا تُخَيِّبَنَّ شُخُوْصِيْ وَوِفَادَتِيْ\nWA LAA TUKHAYYIBANNA SHUKHOOSEE WA WIFAADATEE\nand not to disparage my presence and coming,\nفَقَدْ اَنْفَدْتُ نَفَقَتِيْ\nFAQAD ANFADTU NAFAQATEE\nbecause I have spent all my disbursement,\nوَاَتْعَبْتُ بَدَنِيْ\nWA AT'ABTU BADANEE\ncaused fatigue to my body,\nوَقَطَعْتُ الْمَفَازَاتِ\nWA QATA'TUL MAFAAZAAT\ncrossed deserts,\nوَخَلَّفْتُ الْاَهْلَ وَالْمَالَ وَمَا خَوَّلْتَنِيْ\nWA KHALLAFTUL AHLA WAL MAALA WA MAA KHAWWALTANEE\nleft my family, properties, and whatever You have put under my disposal,\nوَاٰثَرْتُ مَا عِنْدَكَ عَلٰى نَفْسِيْ\nWA AATHARTU MAA I'NDAKA A'LAA NAFSEE\npreferred that which You have to myself,\nوَلُذْتُ بِقَبْرِ عَمِّ نَبِيِّكَ\nWA LUDHTU BIQABRI A'MMI NABIYYIK\nand here I am seeking refuge in the tomb of Your Prophet’s uncle,\nصَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهِ\nSALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIH\nmay peace be upon Your Prophet and his Household,\nوَتَقَرَّبْتُ بِهِ ابْتِغَاۤءَ مَرْضَاتِكَ\nWA TAQARRABTU BIHIB TIGHAA'A MARDAATIK\nand sought his nearness—all that has been in the hope of gaining Your pleasure.\nفَعُدْ بِحِلْمِكَ عَلٰى جَهْلِيْ\nFA'UD BIHILMIKA A'LAA JAHLEE\nSo, (please) confer upon my unreason with Your forbearance\nوَبِرَاْفَتِكَ عَلٰى ذَنْبِيْ\nWA BIRA'FATIKA A'LAA DHANBEE\nand upon my sins with Your kindness,\nفَقَدْ عَظُمَ جُرْمِيْ\nFAQAD A'ZUMA JURMEE\nfor my offense is grave.\nبِرَحْمَتِكَ يَا كَرِيْمُ يَا كَرِيْمُ\nBIRAHMATIKA YAA KAREEMU YAA KAREEM\n(Please do that for me) in the name of Your mercy, O All-generous! O All-generous!",
